cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  legsynth: an open reproduction and extension of durability-aware
  Jansen linkage optimization
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it, and cite the paper it
  reproduces (listed under references below).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gabriel
    family-names: Cantare
    email: gabocantare@gmail.com
    affiliation: Texas A&M University
repository-code: "https://github.com/gabocantare-cloud/legsynth"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-07"
keywords:
  - Jansen linkage
  - strandbeest
  - mechanism synthesis
  - multi-objective optimization
  - NSGA-II
  - Archard wear
  - transmission angle
  - kinematics
abstract: >-
  An open-source reproduction and extension of Wang (2026), which
  re-optimizes Theo Jansen's eleven-bar walking linkage to trade gait
  quality against joint wear and for which no code was released. The
  package implements the full pipeline - dyad-cascade kinematics,
  quasi-static inverse dynamics verified by virtual work, Archard wear
  per revolute joint, and NSGA-II over the ten link lengths - and adds
  the manufacturability check the paper omits: minimum transmission
  angle enforced while the foot is loaded. It publishes explicit
  formulas for the five gait metrics the paper reports but never
  defines, and documents three measured disagreements with the paper's
  numbers rather than tuning them away.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Durability-Aware Multi-Objective Optimization of the Jansen
      Linkage: Trading Gait Quality Against Joint Wear
